% ============================================================================
% meningitis-abx — empiric antibiotic SELECTION for acute bacterial meningitis.
% ============================================================================
% MYCIN-2026 (therapy layer). This is MYCIN's original purpose — recommend the
% therapy — rebuilt on the byte-provenance substrate: grounded, auditable, and
% one-edit-correctable. Each REGIMEN COMPONENT is a hypothesis the engine decides
% to INCLUDE, driven by the patient's factors as deterministic (saturating) rules.
% Reading each component's posterior (independently) gives the empiric regimen.
%
% Grounded in IDSA practice guidelines for bacterial meningitis (Tunkel AR et al.,
% Clin Infect Dis 2004;39:1267) + adjunctive dexamethasone (de Gans & van de Beek,
% NEJM 2002). Citations are authored-from-guideline; spider byte-verification is a
% follow-up (as for the diagnostic clauses). The renal dose + the door-to-
% antibiotic time window are solved separately by the constraint solver (select_abx.py).

dictionary abx_vocab {
    % --- regimen components (the therapy decisions) ---
    define give_vancomycin : hypothesis
    define give_ceftriaxone : hypothesis
    define give_ampicillin : hypothesis
    define give_betalactam_sparing_alt : hypothesis
    define give_dexamethasone : hypothesis

    % --- patient factors (the rule inputs) ---
    define meningitis_dx : finding values [empiric, confirmed]
        surface "suspected bacterial meningitis", "empiric meningitis treatment"
    define age_band : finding values [over_50, under_50]
        surface "age over 50", "older adult", "younger adult"
    define immunocompromised : finding values [yes, no]
        surface "immunocompromised", "HIV", "transplant", "on immunosuppression"
    define betalactam_allergy : finding values [severe, none]
        surface "severe penicillin allergy", "anaphylaxis to beta-lactam", "no drug allergy"
    define suspected_pneumococcal : finding values [yes, no]
        surface "gram-positive diplococci", "pneumococcal", "S. pneumoniae"
}

rulebook meningitis_abx {
    use abx_vocab

    % VANCOMYCIN — always, empirically (covers penicillin-resistant S. pneumoniae).
    prior 0.02 for give_vancomycin   source "IDSA Tunkel 2004 (empiric vancomycin)" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from meningitis_dx(empiric) to give_vancomycin
        source "IDSA 2004: empiric vancomycin for resistant pneumococcus" trust authoritative

    % CEFTRIAXONE (3rd-gen cephalosporin) — base coverage, UNLESS a severe
    % beta-lactam allergy, which drags its inclusion back down (the exclusion).
    prior 0.02 for give_ceftriaxone   source "IDSA Tunkel 2004 (3rd-gen cephalosporin)" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from meningitis_dx(empiric) to give_ceftriaxone
        source "IDSA 2004: empiric 3rd-gen cephalosporin" trust authoritative
    contributes 0.0000001 from betalactam_allergy(severe) to give_ceftriaxone
        source "IDSA 2004: avoid beta-lactams in severe/anaphylactic allergy" trust authoritative

    % AMPICILLIN — add for Listeria cover if age > 50 OR immunocompromised.
    prior 0.02 for give_ampicillin   source "IDSA Tunkel 2004 (Listeria cover)" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from age_band(over_50) to give_ampicillin
        source "IDSA 2004: add ampicillin (Listeria) for age >50" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from immunocompromised(yes) to give_ampicillin
        source "IDSA 2004: add ampicillin (Listeria) if immunocompromised" trust authoritative

    % BETA-LACTAM-SPARING ALTERNATIVE — when the cephalosporin is excluded by allergy.
    prior 0.02 for give_betalactam_sparing_alt   source "IDSA Tunkel 2004 (alt regimen)" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from betalactam_allergy(severe) to give_betalactam_sparing_alt
        source "IDSA 2004: moxifloxacin/aztreonam (+ TMP-SMX for Listeria) if severe beta-lactam allergy" trust authoritative

    % DEXAMETHASONE — adjunct, with/before the first antibiotic dose, if pneumococcal.
    prior 0.02 for give_dexamethasone   source "de Gans & van de Beek, NEJM 2002" trust authoritative
    contributes 1000000 from suspected_pneumococcal(yes) to give_dexamethasone
        source "NEJM 2002 / IDSA 2004: adjunct dexamethasone for suspected pneumococcal meningitis" trust authoritative
}

? give_vancomycin
? give_ceftriaxone
? give_ampicillin
? give_betalactam_sparing_alt
? give_dexamethasone
